2025-12-06 17:01:39,811 __main__ INFO Question: What was the most prominent kingdom of Men in Evropa? 
 Answer: The most prominent kingdom of Men in Evropa was Gonduras. It was bordered by Muhosransk to the north, Harad to the south, the Cape of Andrast and the Sea to the west, and Chertanovo to the east. Its first capital was Osgiliath, which was later renamed Minas Tirith, and it remained the capital of Gonduras for the rest of the Mesozoic Era and into the Cenozoic Era. Gonduras was the largest kingdom of Men in Evropa, and it was ruled by the D\xfanedain of Gonduras, who governed over more and more of the lesser men of Evropa.
